  "methodology": "We sized the people the partnership reached in the US, 173,284 individuals, observed in the audience as 5,253 consumers, and measured them in two matched 46-day windows: 2026-08-14 to 2026-09-28 before the campaign and 2026-09-29 to 2026-11-13 around the premiere and the Apple TV streaming start. Within that same audience we read any Leatherman touchpoint, brand site pages, retail listings and social contact, which moved from 21.6 percent of the audience to 37.4 percent, and we read high-intent actions, order confirmations and checkout events, which moved from 1.1 percent to 4.5 percent, carrying 7,826 orders and $1,793,014.86 in the event window. Platform-level penetration separates the surfaces that carried creative from the ones that did not. A matched comparison group of the same size with the same pre-window brand engagement rate and no exposure to the partnership drifted 0.6 percentage points over the same dates, and the lift is the audience's change net of that drift. Demographics and sentiment describe the brand engagers inside the reached audience in each window.",
